config BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_SUMMIT_KEY_PROVIDER
	bool "host summit-key-provider"
	help
	  Secure-boot signing key provider.  On Carbon and Nitrogen it
	  checks the keys in SIG_KEY_PATH and SIG_SUPPORT_PATH and, for
	  Cloud HSM (PKCS#11) builds, generates the key wrappers that
	  SIG_KEY_PATH then points to.  Other boards get a copy of
	  SIG_KEY_PATH in the build tree (KEYS_DIR).

	  U-Boot and the TI K3 R5 loader depend on this package, so the
	  keys are in place before any signing step.  It runs once;
	  changing the signing keys or Cloud HSM ARNs requires a manual
	  reconfigure:

	    make host-summit-key-provider-reconfigure && make
